---
import site from '../data/site.json';

const v = site.validation;

const limits = [
  {
    title: 'Particle-laden samples',
    detail: 'Samples 5 and 7 both needed non-standard handling. Suspended particles clogged the membranes of sample 5, and only ~80 mL of the 100 mL sample was pulled through. Sample 7 is a spiked positive control and not a field sample. Both samples are implicated in the classification disagreements described in Validation.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Non-identical manifold construction',
    detail: `The ABS manifold used a fully 3D-printed funnel. The rPET manifold used a commercial Millipore funnel on a printed base. If a printed funnel traps bacteria more readily than a steel one, the all-printed manifold would be expected to read systematically low. Consistent with this, the ABS manifold returned the lowest count of the three manifolds at 6 of the 8 sites (sites 1-6). At site 7, the rPET manifold (with its commercial funnel) read lowest instead, and that comparison is also the sole classification mismatch. At site 8, all three manifolds tied at the detection floor.`,
  },
  {
    title: 'Single operator and single testing season',
    detail: `All ${v.filtrations} filtrations were run by one person across one testing period. Neither operator variability nor seasonal variation in source water is captured.`,
  },
  {
    title: 'Non-randomised filtration order',
    detail: 'The manifolds were run in blocks. On each of the two test days, all 12 filtrations of that day\'s four samples were done on the rPET manifold, then on the ABS manifold, then on the Millipore reference. Particles may have settled, or bacteria grown during storage, while the printed manifolds were run first. Either effect could inflate the reference counts relative to the printed manifolds.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Sample storage and plate reading',
    detail: 'All samples were collected on 31 May 2026 and stored in dim light without refrigeration. They were filtered 1 to 2 days later. The funnels of all three manifolds, including the commercial Millipore funnels, were reused after an alcohol wipe. Plates were read once, at 24 h, by the operator, who knew which manifold each plate came from. Small colonies on plates with particles or algae were hard to tell apart.',
  },
];
---
<section id="limits">
  <div class="eyebrow">Limitations</div>
  <h2>Limitations</h2>
  <p class="lead">
    3DPLAM is an open, locally 3D-printable alternative route to the same
    measurement the Millipore EZ-Fit performs. 3DPLAM was validated
    against that instrument as a reference. The validation does not show
    that the two are identical.
  </p>

  <ul class="limits-list">
    {limits.map((l) => (
      <li>
        <strong>{l.title}</strong>
        <span>{l.detail}</span>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>
</section>

<style>
  .limits-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 24px 0 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 14px;
  }
  .limits-list li {
    padding: 20px 22px;
    background: var(--bg-2);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--ghe-red);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0;
  }
  .limits-list strong {
    display: block;
    color: var(--fg);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 15.5px;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .limits-list span {
    display: block;
    color: var(--fg-dim);
    font-size: 14.5px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
</style>
